  'II. Anand: 1. bothersome  2. creative  3. confident | Anita: 1. responsible  2. curious  3. careful',
  'III. 1. A rush of thefts in the colony – he felt a burglar alarm was needed.',
  '2. The alarm was rigged to work when the door was opened gently; Papa always opens the door softly, so the water bag fell on him.',
  '3. Papa – angry and strict (locked his tool box, said NO); Ma – soothing and sympathetic but watchful; Anita – sceptical and unwilling, yet she helps.',
  '4. He took apart the gadgets in the house for parts, made a lot of noise hammering and sawing, let no one into his room and forgot even to comb his hair.',
  '5. A time machine seemed impossible; he thought it was a child’s imagination and that the thief had simply run out.',
  '6. (Model) Boppa pressed a switch and found himself in the Kolkata of a hundred years ago. Frightened and alone, he promised never to steal again – and became an honest sweeper in the past.',
